WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.340
What’s good y’all?

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:24.600
This week we sip sip sippin with "The Cask of Amontillado" by Edgar Allan Poe, my man.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.820
Da narrator of this story got major beef
with some fool named Fortunato.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.060
He been burned so bad by this cat dat he ain’t bout to let it slide.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.740
Dat hater has got to go.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.460
Da narrator wanna get revenge, but he ain’t
gonna just ghost a brutha in broad daylight.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:46.160
So he start thinkin, “If there’s one thing I know bout dat bitch, it’s that he love to get his drink on.”

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.660
So he decide to use Fortunato’s mad love for wine to GIT DAT SUCKA.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.880
So da narrator roll up to Fortunato while he shit-faced at a carnival.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:01.840
Boy like, “Say dawg. I got a bottle of da cleanest wine you ever seen back at my place — might even be Amontillado.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.660
If you don’t want a taste,
I guess I could sip wit my boy Luchesi...”

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.360
“Yo hold up playboy — Luchesi don’t know Amontillado from his assh*le. Let's do this."

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:15.960
So da narrator take Fortunato to his family
crypt, where he keep his stash of expensive bottles.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.600
But da place all full of nitre, and Fortunato start coughin like a little ol' bitch.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.120
Da narrator like, “Look if you can’t hang, we can just forget about it.”

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.870
But Fortunato like, “Naw bruh — I'm straight.”

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.380
Fool straight fiendin fo that Amontillado.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:35.800
As they go deeper into da catacombs, da narrator make sure he keep Fortunato nice and liquored up.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:42.140
These vaults got dead bodies from da narrator’s
bloodline, AKA the Montresor fam, by the stack.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:48.080
He start talkin bout his people's coat of arms and their hard-ass motto: “No one attacks me with impunity.”

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.840
Lata, Fortunato throw up a mason gang sign,
but Montresor don’t recognize what da hell he doin.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.220
Fortunato like, “Oh, you ain’t a mason?”

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.980
Montresor: “Oh fo sho, fo sho I’m a Mason.”

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:02.380
But when Montresor can’t prove he legit, he start feelin like a real scrub.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:06.920
Eventually, they roll up on a little hole
in the wall, and Montressor like,

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.760
“Well, there it is. Go in there and po up some Amontillado.”

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:18.280
Since Fortunato's wasted as hell by now, he ain’t even trip when Montresor chain his body to da damn wall.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.980
Then brutha start layin bricks, trapping Fortunato in dat baby-sized room.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.540
At first, Fortunato don’t know what da hell goin on.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:31.180
Just as Montresor lay dat last brick, he hear da bells on Fortunato’s hat.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:36.420
And fo fifty years after, Fortunato’s body still chillin in dem chains.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:42.760
May he rest in peace... I guess?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:49.780
The realest scholars be all up on this text’s nuts, sayin it’s Poe’s most perfect short story, since its strapped with irony.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.080
Fo one, there’s some dramatic irony at the core of the plot:

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.660
Da reader know that Fortunato bout to get wrecked, but Fortunato ain’t got a clue what’s coming.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.838
On top of dat, Poe slangin verbal irony like he don’t give a f**k.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.920
Da name Fortunato means “da fortunate one,” and dat cat is far from lucky —

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.040
unless gettin tho’d and buried alive is yo thang.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.540
Almost everything dat come outta Montresor’s mouth when he conversatin with Fortunato

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.620
got a different meaning from what he actually say.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:23.340
Even though he want Fortunato to keep sippin his juice and cruisin deeper in to the vaults, he always saying sh*t like,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.459
“Nah, bruh — let’s go back.”

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:29.779
“‘Come,’ I said, with decision, ‘we will go back; your health is precious.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:34.808
You are rich, respected, admired, beloved; you are happy as once I was.

00:03:34.808 --> 00:03:36.720
You are a man to be missed.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:42.180
For me it is no matter. We will
go back; you will be ill, and I cannot be responsible...’”

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:48.480
But he know damn well dat Fortunato ain’t gonna back down, since he jonesin fo dat sweet Amontillado.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.880
Even Fortunato’s stupid ass hat got irony to it.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:57.540
Da last thing Montresor hear after he hole dat hater up is da jingle of them damn bells.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.580
See, back in Poe’s day, peeps would put bells on da limbs of dead rich folk

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.340
so they don’t accidentally bury them alive.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:10.480
'Cept this time, when da bells start jinglin, ain’t nobody comin to help — specially not God.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.804
The last words Montresor say before he finish the wall?

00:04:13.804 --> 00:04:15.430
“Yes for the love of God!”

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.391
But he sho as hell ain’t doin it for da love of God.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.840
What he is doin it for, though, is revenge.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.320
Sh*t, dat lust fo vengeance might even run through his veins.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.520
I mean, da family motto is, "No one provokes me with impunity,” or in real talk:

00:04:29.528 --> 00:04:31.660
"Don’t f**k wit me or it ain’t gonna be pretty."

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.580
Actually, da hell did Fortunato even do?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.900
Montresor never give us the lowdown.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.340
I mean, it gotta be something whack if he came up with such a crazy-ass plan to kill him.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.460
Then again, maybe Fortunato actually didn’t do sh*t.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:47.840
Maybe Montresor just hatin to rep them family values.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.980
Check out what some scholarly hood named Thompson say:

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:56.280
“Montresor's lack of remorse, then, even
after fifty years, should not be a wonder to us...

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:02.800
He has an obligation to his family; he carries it out, with relish, and savors deeply the satisfaction that success

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:08.280
in carrying out this obligation brings him. ... [W]hat he did, he is convinced, was justified.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:13.520
He was carrying out an obligation to his family as he saw it — as he was culturally conditioned to see it.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.700
Now, fifty years after the event, he can recount it with pride.”

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:22.660
All I know is dat if some fool named Montresor
come trippin to yo face, just walk away, homie.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.260
Cuz dem cats don’t play.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:30.860
Yo, if you're feelin your boy Poe, then take a minute to click on this dumbass bird to be taken to my episode on "The Raven."

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.520
Catch ya later playas.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.000
Peace!

